<title>INDIA: India's SBI H1 96/97 net seen sharply up.</title>
<headline>India's SBI H1 96/97 net seen sharply up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State Bank of India (SBI) is expected to post a 177.7 percent increase in its net profit for the half year ended September 30, 1996, according to a Reuters poll of 14 securities and brokerage firms.</p>
<p>Analysts' forecasts of the net profit ranged from a low of 5.14 billion rupees to a high of 7.5 billion rupees.</p>
<p>The average of the forecasts worked out to 6.4 billion rupees, representing a 177.7 percent growth over the 2.3 billion figure recorded for the half year ended September 30, 1995.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SBI  ----PAT seen up 177.7%, income up 22.5%</p>
<p>				 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		 INCOME</p>
<p>			 H1 96/97  H1 95/96     H1 96/97   H1 95/96</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Average		6,399.13  2,304.00    76,605.14  62,520.30</p>
<p>High		   7,500.00		  86,124.00</p>
<p>Low		    5,144.00		  59,850.00</p>
